#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bin/hook-trace [<transcript>] [--last] [--session <id>] [--days <n>] [--main-only] [--check]

One line per hook fire, joined from the two records a fire leaves behind. Both have
always existed; nothing had ever read them together (#205).

  our row        `~/.claude/logs/<hook>-<day>.jsonl`, written by `_hook.run_row()`. The
                 hook's self-report: that it ran, what it decided (`verdict`), what it
                 was looking at (`exposed`, a guard slug), and what it cost (`seconds`).
                 It is the only record a silent fire leaves at all, and it stops at the
                 hook's own process exit, so it can say "I refused" and never say
                 whether the refusal held.
  the harness's  the session transcript, written by Claude Code itself. It holds the
                 other half: which channel the text went out on, which audience saw it,
                 how long the harness waited, and what happened next.

`bin/hook-report` divides the rows into rates; this joins them to the behaviour. A row
proves the fire, the transcript proves the outcome.

THE HARNESS'S SCHEMA
--------------------
Undocumented, and this docstring is the only place on this machine it is written down:
`bin/hook-trace` is the reader, the skills point here rather than caching a copy, and
`hooks/test_hook_trace.py` fails with the field named when a Claude Code version
renames one. Measured 2026-09-04 over the last 150 sessions, Claude Code 2.1.259 and
2.1.260.

A transcript is one JSON object per line at
`~/.claude/projects/<project>/<sessionId>.jsonl`. A subagent gets its own file,
`~/.claude/projects/<project>/<sessionId>/subagents/agent-<agentId>.jsonl`, whose
records carry `agentId` and `isSidechain: true` and the *parent's* `sessionId`, which is
the only session id a subagent's hooks are handed and therefore the only one its rows
can carry. Envelope fields read here: `type` and `subtype`, `timestamp` (UTC,
milliseconds, trailing `Z`; our rows are local seconds, so every comparison converts),
`agentId` (which agent a fire belongs to, taken from the record rather than the file it
sits in), `message`, `isMeta` and `toolDenialKind` (the outcome records below). The
session is the transcript's own filename, which is what `sessionId` holds on every
record and what every run row carries; the envelope's *other* id, `session_id`, is
deliberately not read, since it names neither.

`type: "attachment"`, keyed by `attachment.type`. `hookEvent` is the event
(`PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `PermissionRequest`); `hookName` is the
*registration* (`PreToolUse:Bash`, `Stop`), never the script, so a fire is attributed to
a hook by its `command` where one is recorded and otherwise by the `[hook]` prefix every
channel on this machine opens with (#197):

  hook_success            `command`, `stdout`, `stderr`, `exitCode`, `durationMs`,
                          `content`, `toolUseID`. Written only when the hook spoke: 108
                          of 872 Stop fires carried one and no `PreToolUse:Bash` fire
                          did, so its absence is not evidence a hook did not run.
  hook_cancelled          `command`, `durationMs`, `timedOut`, `timeoutMs`, `toolUseID`
                          (all but `toolUseID` absent on 1 of the 4 in the corpus).
  hook_blocking_error     `blockingError.blockingError`: the text the agent saw as a
                          block. No `command`.
  hook_additional_context `content`, a *list* of strings: the text the agent saw as
                          context. No `command`.
  hook_system_message     `content`, a string: the line the human saw. The one record
                          that separates the two audiences. No `command`.
  hook_non_blocking_error `stderr`, `stdout`, `exitCode`, `command`, `durationMs`: a
                          hook that exited 1.
  hook_permission_decision `decision`, `toolUseID`, `hookEvent: "PermissionRequest"`.
                          The one record type that names neither hook nor command, so a
                          PermissionRequest fire takes its name from the row it joins.

`type: "system"`:

  subtype stop_hook_summary   one per Stop, and the only record that names the *silent*
                              fires: `hookInfos[{command, durationMs}]` for every Stop
                              hook registered, plus `hookCount`, `hookErrors`,
                              `hookAdditionalContext`, `preventedContinuation`,
                              `stopReason`, `hasOutput`, `toolUseID`.
                              `preventedContinuation` was `false` on all 1,150 summaries
                              in the corpus, including every one carrying a block, so it
                              is read and printed but never believed: the turn's fate is
                              taken from what follows the summary.
  subtype informational       `content`, the block-cap override ("A hook blocked the
                              turn from ending N consecutive times").

The two records that carry the outcome, both written by the harness for the agent:

  a `user` record whose `message.content[]` holds a `tool_result` with `tool_use_id`,
  `is_error`, and (on a hook refusal) `toolDenialKind` on the envelope. `is_error` alone
  is a tool that ran and failed; `toolDenialKind` is the deny. Two values measured on
  this machine: `permission-rule`, a hook's own refusal, and `user-rejected`, a person
  declining in the UI, whose `content` is the harness's own boilerplate ("The user
  doesn't want to proceed…") and names no hook at all (#209) — only the first builds a
  fire from the `tool_result` alone.

  a `user` record whose `message.content` is the string `Stop hook feedback:\\n<reason>`
  (`isMeta: true`): a Stop block, as the agent received it.

Inside a subagent, a `permission-rule` PreToolUse deny writes no `hook_system_message` at
all (#209): the `tool_result` above is the *only* record, its own `content` carrying the
hook's text where an attachment would otherwise have carried it. Read there and nowhere
else, that text is what names the fire and fills its one channel, printed as `agent` since
a record with no attachment can prove only that the agent, not a person, saw it.

THE JOIN
--------
`sessionId` plus `toolUseID` on the tool events: `_hook.run_row()` stamps the payload's
`tool_use_id` (#205), which PreToolUse and PostToolUse carry and Stop does not. Where
one side has no id (a Stop fire, or a row written before #205), the fall-back is nearest
timestamp within the same session, event and hook, paired nearest-first so two fires of
the same hook in the same second cannot both claim one record.

THE COLUMNS
-----------
  hook      the script, from `command`, the `[hook]` prefix, or a bare `hook:` prefix
            (#209, gauntlet's own shape); `?` where the harness named none of those and
            no row joined.
  event     `hookEvent`, or our row's `event` for a fire only the row saw.
  agent     `main`, or the subagent's `agentId`. `--main-only` drops the subagents.
  verdict   our row's word. `-` means no row: the harness saw a fire we did not record.
  channel   what the harness routed, `context`/`block`/`agent`/`system`/`stderr`/
            `stdout`/`cancelled`/`permission`. `agent` is a `tool_result`-only deny with
            no attachment at all (#209). `-` is a silent fire.
  audience  `agent`, `human`, or `both`, from those channels. The question
            `/audit-doc` asks and no other record answers.
  chars     per channel, in the channel column's order.
  ms        the harness's own `durationMs`, which includes the process the row's
            `seconds` could not measure from inside itself.
  outcome   read from the transcript, never from the verdict: `ran`/`ran-error`/`denied`
            for a gate, `continued`/`ended` for a Stop (the first assistant record or
            human prompt after the summary), the `decision` for a PermissionRequest, and
            `mismatch` where that contradicts the row, the sentence below saying which
            way round.

MISMATCHES
----------
Printed under the table, and `--check` exits 1 if there are any, so the join can run in
a harness rather than be read by a human. Five kinds, each one a place where the two
records disagree about what happened:

  a speaking verdict with no harness record   the hook says it refused or injected and
                                              the transcript holds no trace of it.
  a harness record with no row                the transcript holds text a hook put in
                                              front of someone, and no hook admits it.
  `deny` whose tool ran                       the refusal did not reach the tool.
  a hand-back/`not-mine`/`deferred` whose      #204, generalised by #209: every Stop
  turn continued                              verdict meant to end the turn continues
                                              under the same cap as a block.
  `block` whose turn ended                    the block did not hold (the cap override).

UNATTRIBUTED
------------
Printed once, grouped, below the mismatches: every text neither a `[hook]` prefix nor a
bare `hook:` prefix could name (#209), so a wide `--days` window answers "what is this
`?`" in one line instead of a grep. Each line is the text's first 40 characters and how
many fires carried it.
"""
import argparse
import bisect
import json
import re
import shlex
import sys
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from datetime import datetime, timedelta
from pathlib import Path

_REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
_HOOKS_DIR = next((c for c in (_REPO_ROOT / "hooks", _REPO_ROOT / ".claude" / "hooks") if c.is_dir()), _REPO_ROOT / "hooks")
sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))

import _harness
import _hook

PROJECTS_DIR = Path.home() / ".claude" / "projects"

MATCH_WINDOW_SECONDS = 300

CANDIDATES_PER_FIRE = 40

SKEW_SAMPLE = 50
SKEW_HOURS = 14
SKEW_MINIMUM = 3

SPEAKING = {"deny", "block", "handback", "not-mine", "deferred", "warn", "stop", "inform", "ask"}

ENDS_TURN = {"handback": "hand-back", "not-mine": "not-mine", "deferred": "deferred"}

CHANNELS = {
    "hook_additional_context": "context",
    "hook_blocking_error": "block",
    "hook_system_message": "system",
    "hook_non_blocking_error": "stderr",
    "hook_success": "stdout",
    "hook_cancelled": "cancelled",
    "hook_permission_decision": "permission",
}
CHANNEL_ORDER = ["context", "block", "agent", "system", "stderr", "stdout", "cancelled",
                 "permission"]
AGENT_CHANNELS = {"context", "block", "agent"}
HUMAN_CHANNELS = {"system", "stderr"}

HOOK_PREFIX_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*\[([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)\]")
HOOK_COLON_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*):")

STOP_FEEDBACK = "Stop hook feedback:"
OVERRIDE_PHRASE = "blocked the turn from ending"


@dataclass
class Fire:
    session: str
    agent: str
    event: str
    hook: str
    tool_use_id: str = ""
    when: datetime | None = None
    index: int = -1
    channels: dict = field(default_factory=dict)
    duration_ms: int | None = None
    timed_out: bool = False
    exit_code: int | None = None
    decision: str = ""
    prevented: bool | None = None
    row: dict | None = None
    outcome: str = "-"
    why: str = ""

    @property
    def audience(self) -> str:
        agent = bool(set(self.channels) & AGENT_CHANNELS)
        human = bool(set(self.channels) & HUMAN_CHANNELS)
        return "both" if agent and human else "agent" if agent else "human" if human else "-"


def parse_args(argv=None):
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="hook-trace", description=__doc__,
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
    )
    parser.add_argument("transcript", nargs="?", default=None,
                        help="a transcript path; its own subagents/ are read with it")
    parser.add_argument("--last", action="store_true", help="the newest transcript")
    parser.add_argument("--session", default=None, help="one session id")
    parser.add_argument("--days", type=int, default=None,
                        help="every session touched in this many days")
    parser.add_argument("--projects-dir", default=None,
                        help=f"read transcripts from here instead of {PROJECTS_DIR}")
    parser.add_argument("--log-dir", default=None,
                        help="read run rows from here instead of ~/.claude/logs")
    parser.add_argument("--main-only", action="store_true",
                        help="drop the subagents' fires")
    parser.add_argument("--check", action="store_true",
                        help="print only the mismatches, and exit 1 if there are any")
    return parser.parse_args(argv)




def transcripts(args) -> list[Path]:
    root = Path(args.projects_dir) if args.projects_dir else PROJECTS_DIR
    if args.transcript:
        return [Path(args.transcript)]
    try:
        found = sorted(root.glob("*/*.jsonl"), key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime)
    except OSError:
        return []
    if args.session:
        return [p for p in found if p.stem == args.session]
    if args.days is not None:
        cutoff = datetime.now().timestamp() - args.days * 86400
        return [p for p in found if p.stat().st_mtime >= cutoff]
    return found[-1:]


def subagent_files(main: Path) -> list[Path]:
    try:
        return sorted((main.parent / main.stem / "subagents").glob("agent-*.jsonl"))
    except OSError:
        return []




def local_time(stamp) -> datetime | None:
    if not isinstance(stamp, str) or not stamp:
        return None
    try:
        parsed = datetime.fromisoformat(stamp.replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return parsed.astimezone().replace(tzinfo=None) if parsed.tzinfo else parsed


def hook_of_command(command) -> str:
    if not isinstance(command, str) or not command.strip():
        return ""
    try:
        tokens = shlex.split(command)
    except ValueError:
        tokens = command.split()
    for token in tokens:
        stem = Path(token).name
        if "." in stem and not stem.startswith("."):
            return canon(Path(stem).stem)
    return canon(Path(tokens[0]).stem) if tokens else ""


def canon(name: str) -> str:
    name = (name or "").strip().lower()
    for suffix in ("-hook", "_hook"):
        if name.endswith(suffix) and len(name) > len(suffix):
            name = name[: -len(suffix)]
    return name


def hook_of_text(text: str) -> str:
    match = HOOK_PREFIX_RE.match(text or "") or HOOK_COLON_RE.match(text or "")
    return canon(match.group(1)) if match else ""


def channel_text(kind: str, attachment: dict) -> str:
    if kind == "hook_blocking_error":
        blocking = attachment.get("blockingError")
        if isinstance(blocking, dict):
            blocking = blocking.get("blockingError")
        return blocking if isinstance(blocking, str) else ""
    if kind == "hook_additional_context":
        content = attachment.get("content")
        if isinstance(content, list):
            return "\n".join(c for c in content if isinstance(c, str))
        return content if isinstance(content, str) else ""
    if kind == "hook_system_message":
        content = attachment.get("content")
        return content if isinstance(content, str) else ""
    if kind in ("hook_success", "hook_non_blocking_error"):
        parts = [attachment.get(f) for f in ("stdout", "stderr")]
        return "".join(p for p in parts if isinstance(p, str))
    return ""


def block_text(content) -> str:
    if isinstance(content, str):
        return content
    if isinstance(content, list):
        return "\n".join(c["text"] for c in content
                         if isinstance(c, dict) and isinstance(c.get("text"), str))
    return ""


class Transcript:

    def __init__(self, session: str):
        self.session = session
        self.fires: dict[tuple, Fire] = {}
        self.results: dict[str, tuple[bool, bool]] = {}
        self.marks: list[tuple[int, str]] = []
        self.overrides: list[str] = []
        self.attached_ids: set[str] = set()
        self.unattributed: list[str] = []
        self.next_index = 0

    def fire(self, agent, event, hook, tool_use_id, when, index) -> Fire:
        key = (agent, event, hook, tool_use_id)
        found = self.fires.get(key)
        if found is None:
            found = Fire(session=self.session, agent=agent, event=event, hook=hook,
                         tool_use_id=tool_use_id, when=when, index=index)
            self.fires[key] = found
        if found.index < 0 or 0 <= index < found.index:
            found.index, found.when = index, when
        return found

    def read(self, path: Path) -> None:
        try:
            handle = path.open(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
        except OSError:
            return
        with handle:
            for line in handle:
                index = self.next_index
                self.next_index += 1
                try:
                    record = json.loads(line)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                if not isinstance(record, dict):
                    continue
                kind = record.get("type")
                if kind == "attachment":
                    self._attachment(record, index)
                elif kind == "system":
                    if record.get("subtype") == "stop_hook_summary":
                        self._summary(record, index)
                    elif record.get("subtype") == "informational":
                        self._informational(record)
                elif kind == "assistant":
                    self.marks.append((index, "assistant"))
                elif kind == "user":
                    self._user(record, index)

    def _attachment(self, record: dict, index: int) -> None:
        agent = record.get("agentId") or "main"
        attachment = record.get("attachment")
        if not isinstance(attachment, dict):
            return
        kind = attachment.get("type")
        if kind not in CHANNELS:
            return
        event = attachment.get("hookEvent") or ""
        text = channel_text(kind, attachment)
        hook = hook_of_command(attachment.get("command")) or hook_of_text(text)
        if not hook and text.strip():
            self.unattributed.append(text)
        when = local_time(record.get("timestamp"))
        tool_use_id = attachment.get("toolUseID") or ""
        fire = self.fire(agent, event, hook, tool_use_id, when, index)
        if tool_use_id:
            self.attached_ids.add(tool_use_id)
        channel = CHANNELS[kind]
        if text.strip() or channel in ("permission", "cancelled"):
            fire.channels[channel] = fire.channels.get(channel, 0) + len(text)
        if isinstance(attachment.get("durationMs"), int):
            fire.duration_ms = attachment["durationMs"]
        if isinstance(attachment.get("exitCode"), int):
            fire.exit_code = attachment["exitCode"]
        if attachment.get("timedOut") is True:
            fire.timed_out = True
        if isinstance(attachment.get("decision"), str):
            fire.decision = attachment["decision"]

    def _summary(self, record: dict, index: int) -> None:
        agent = record.get("agentId") or "main"
        when = local_time(record.get("timestamp"))
        infos = record.get("hookInfos")
        for info in infos if isinstance(infos, list) else []:
            if not isinstance(info, dict):
                continue
            fire = self.fire(agent, "Stop", hook_of_command(info.get("command")),
                             record.get("toolUseID") or "", when, index)
            if fire.duration_ms is None and isinstance(info.get("durationMs"), int):
                fire.duration_ms = info["durationMs"]
            fire.prevented = record.get("preventedContinuation")

    def _informational(self, record: dict) -> None:
        content = record.get("content")
        if isinstance(content, str) and OVERRIDE_PHRASE in content:
            self.overrides.append(content)

    def _user(self, record: dict, index: int) -> None:
        message = record.get("message")
        content = (message or {}).get("content") if isinstance(message, dict) else None
        if isinstance(content, list):
            results = [b for b in content
                       if isinstance(b, dict) and b.get("type") == "tool_result"]
            kind = record.get("toolDenialKind")
            for block in results:
                tool_use_id = block.get("tool_use_id")
                if isinstance(tool_use_id, str) and tool_use_id:
                    self.results[tool_use_id] = (block.get("is_error") is True, bool(kind))
                    if kind == "permission-rule":
                        self._denial_fire(record, block, tool_use_id, index)
            if results:
                return
        if isinstance(content, str) and content.startswith(STOP_FEEDBACK):
            return
        if record.get("isMeta") is True:
            return
        self.marks.append((index, "prompt"))

    def _denial_fire(self, record: dict, block: dict, tool_use_id: str, index: int) -> None:
        if tool_use_id in self.attached_ids:
            return
        text = block_text(block.get("content"))
        hook = hook_of_text(text)
        if not hook and text.strip():
            self.unattributed.append(text)
        agent = record.get("agentId") or "main"
        when = local_time(record.get("timestamp"))
        fire = self.fire(agent, "PreToolUse", hook, tool_use_id, when, index)
        if text.strip():
            fire.channels["agent"] = fire.channels.get("agent", 0) + len(text)

    def turn_after(self, index: int) -> str:
        for at, kind in self.marks:
            if at > index:
                return "continued" if kind == "assistant" else "ended"
        return "-"

    def outcome(self, fire: Fire) -> str:
        if fire.event == "Stop":
            return self.turn_after(fire.index) if fire.index >= 0 else "-"
        if fire.event == "PermissionRequest":
            return fire.decision or "-"
        result = self.results.get(fire.tool_use_id)
        if result is None:
            return "-"
        is_error, denied = result
        return "denied" if denied else "ran-error" if is_error else "ran"


def read_session(main: Path, main_only: bool) -> Transcript:
    transcript = Transcript(main.stem)
    transcript.read(main)
    if not main_only:
        for path in subagent_files(main):
            transcript.read(path)
    return transcript




def row_time(row: dict) -> datetime | None:
    try:
        return datetime.fromisoformat(row["ts"]) if isinstance(row.get("ts"), str) else None
    except ValueError:
        return None


def join(fires: list[Fire], rows: list[dict]) -> list[dict]:
    by_id: dict[str, Fire] = {}
    for fire in fires:
        if fire.tool_use_id:
            by_id.setdefault(fire.tool_use_id, fire)
    spare = []
    for row in rows:
        fire = by_id.get(row.get("tool_use_id"))
        if fire is not None and fire.row is None and _compatible(fire, row):
            fire.row = row
        else:
            spare.append(row)

    buckets: dict[str, list[tuple[datetime, int, dict]]] = {}
    for n, row in enumerate(spare):
        when = row_time(row)
        if when is not None:
            buckets.setdefault(row.get("event") or "", []).append((when, n, row))
    for bucket in buckets.values():
        bucket.sort(key=lambda entry: entry[:2])

    pairs = []
    for n, fire in enumerate(fires):
        if fire.row is not None or fire.when is None:
            continue
        for gap, index, row in _candidates(fire, buckets):
            pairs.append((int(gap), _affinity(fire, row), gap, n, index, fire, row))
    taken_rows, taken_fires = set(), set()
    for *_, fire_n, row_index, fire, row in sorted(pairs, key=lambda pair: pair[:5]):
        if fire_n in taken_fires or row_index in taken_rows:
            continue
        fire.row = row
        taken_fires.add(fire_n)
        taken_rows.add(row_index)
    return [row for n, row in enumerate(spare) if n not in taken_rows]


def _affinity(fire: Fire, row: dict) -> tuple[int, int]:
    spoke = any(fire.channels.get(c) for c in AGENT_CHANNELS | HUMAN_CHANNELS)
    row_hook = canon(row.get("hook") or row.get("tool") or "")
    return (0 if spoke == ((row.get("verdict") or "") in SPEAKING) else 1,
            0 if fire.hook and fire.hook == row_hook else 1)


def _candidates(fire: Fire, buckets: dict[str, list]) -> list[tuple]:
    found = []
    for event in dict.fromkeys((fire.event, "")):
        found.extend(_walk(fire, buckets.get(event) or []))
    return found


def _walk(fire: Fire, bucket: list[tuple[datetime, int, dict]]) -> list[tuple]:
    at = bisect.bisect_left(bucket, (fire.when,))
    left, right, found = at - 1, at, []
    while len(found) < CANDIDATES_PER_FIRE and (left >= 0 or right < len(bucket)):
        take_left = right >= len(bucket) or (
            left >= 0 and (fire.when - bucket[left][0]) <= (bucket[right][0] - fire.when))
        when, index, row = bucket[left] if take_left else bucket[right]
        left, right = (left - 1, right) if take_left else (left, right + 1)
        gap = abs((fire.when - when).total_seconds())
        if gap > MATCH_WINDOW_SECONDS:
            break
        if _compatible(fire, row):
            found.append((gap, index, row))
    return found


def clock_skews(fires: list[Fire], spare: list[dict]) -> dict[tuple, int]:
    joined = {(f.hook, f.event) for f in fires if f.row is not None}
    unmatched: dict[tuple, list[datetime]] = {}
    for fire in fires:
        if fire.row is None and fire.when is not None:
            if (fire.hook, fire.event) not in joined:
                unmatched.setdefault((fire.hook, fire.event), []).append(fire.when)
    for times in unmatched.values():
        times.sort()
    sampled: dict[tuple, list[datetime]] = {}
    for row in spare:
        key = (canon(row.get("hook") or row.get("tool") or ""), row.get("event") or "")
        when = row_time(row)
        if when is not None and key in unmatched and len(sampled.get(key, ())) < SKEW_SAMPLE:
            sampled.setdefault(key, []).append(when)

    skews = {}
    for key, times in sampled.items():
        best, hits = 0, 0
        for hours in range(-SKEW_HOURS, SKEW_HOURS + 1):
            if not hours:
                continue
            shift = timedelta(hours=hours)
            aligned = sum(1 for when in times if _near(unmatched[key], when - shift))
            if aligned > hits:
                best, hits = hours, aligned
        if hits >= max(SKEW_MINIMUM, len(times) // 2):
            skews[key] = best
    return skews


def _near(times: list[datetime], when: datetime) -> bool:
    at = bisect.bisect_left(times, when)
    return any(abs((when - t).total_seconds()) <= MATCH_WINDOW_SECONDS
               for t in times[max(0, at - 1):at + 1])


def _compatible(fire: Fire, row: dict) -> bool:
    if row.get("session_id") != fire.session:
        return False
    row_event = row.get("event") or ""
    if row_event and row_event != fire.event:
        return False
    row_hook = canon(row.get("hook") or row.get("tool") or "")
    return not fire.hook or not row_hook or fire.hook == row_hook




def mismatch(fire: Fire, skews: dict[tuple, int] | None = None) -> str:
    row, verdict = fire.row, (fire.row or {}).get("verdict") or ""
    spoke = [c for c, chars in fire.channels.items() if chars]
    if row is None:
        if not spoke:
            return ""
        hours = (skews or {}).get((fire.hook, fire.event))
        return (f"the harness recorded {'+'.join(sorted(spoke))} and no hook wrote a row "
                "for it" + (f", though that hook's rows are stamped {hours:+d}h from its "
                            "fires: two writers, two clocks" if hours else ""))
    if verdict in ("deny", "block") and fire.event != "Stop" and fire.outcome == "ran":
        return f"row says {verdict!r} and the tool ran"
    if not fire.channels and fire.index < 0 and verdict in SPEAKING:
        return f"row says {verdict!r} and the transcript holds no record of it"
    released = row.get("released") or verdict
    if fire.event == "Stop":
        label = ENDS_TURN.get(released)
        if label and fire.outcome == "continued":
            return f"{label} continued the turn instead of ending it (#204)"
        if released == "block" and fire.outcome == "ended":
            return "block did not hold: the turn ended anyway"
    return ""


def group_unattributed(texts: list[str]) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:
    counts: dict[str, int] = {}
    order: list[str] = []
    for text in texts:
        prefix = text[:40]
        if prefix not in counts:
            order.append(prefix)
        counts[prefix] = counts.get(prefix, 0) + 1
    return sorted(((p, counts[p]) for p in order), key=lambda pc: (-pc[1], pc[0]))




def cells(fire: Fire) -> list[str]:
    channels = [c for c in CHANNEL_ORDER if c in fire.channels]
    row = fire.row or {}
    return [
        fire.hook or canon(row.get("hook") or row.get("tool") or "") or "?",
        fire.event or row.get("event") or "-",
        fire.agent,
        row.get("verdict") or "-",
        "+".join(channels) or "-",
        fire.audience,
        "+".join(str(fire.channels[c]) for c in channels) or "-",
        "-" if fire.duration_ms is None else str(fire.duration_ms),
        "mismatch" if fire.why else
        (fire.outcome + " timeout") if fire.timed_out else fire.outcome,
    ]


def render(fires: list[Fire]) -> list[str]:
    header = ["hook", "event", "agent", "verdict", "channel", "audience", "chars", "ms",
              "outcome"]
    lines = ["| " + " | ".join(header) + " |", "|" + "---|" * len(header)]
    for fire in fires:
        lines.append("| " + " | ".join(cells(fire)) + " |")
    return lines


def main(argv=None) -> int:
    args = parse_args(argv)
    paths = transcripts(args)
    if not paths:
        print("No transcript selected. Try --last, --session <id>, --days <n>, or a path.")
        return 0

    log_dir = Path(args.log_dir) if args.log_dir else _hook.LOG_DIR
    rows = [r for r in _harness.rows(log_dir, days=_hook.LOG_RETENTION_DAYS)
            if (r.get("event") or "") != "bin"]
    retained = datetime.now() - timedelta(days=_hook.LOG_RETENTION_DAYS)
    by_session: dict[str, list[dict]] = {}
    for row in rows:
        by_session.setdefault(row.get("session_id") or "", []).append(row)

    fires: list[Fire] = []
    orphan_rows: list[dict] = []
    unattributed: list[str] = []
    skews: dict[tuple, int] = {}
    for path in paths:
        transcript = read_session(path, args.main_only)
        found = sorted(transcript.fires.values(), key=lambda f: f.index)
        for fire in found:
            fire.outcome = transcript.outcome(fire)
        spare = join(found, by_session.get(transcript.session, []))
        skews.update(clock_skews(found, spare))
        unattributed.extend(transcript.unattributed)
        for row in spare:
            orphan = Fire(session=transcript.session, agent="main",
                          event=row.get("event") or "", hook=canon(row.get("hook") or ""),
                          tool_use_id=row.get("tool_use_id") or "", when=row_time(row),
                          row=row)
            orphan.outcome = transcript.outcome(orphan)
            orphan_rows.append(orphan)
            found.append(orphan)
        fires.extend(found)
        for text in transcript.overrides:
            print(f"override: {transcript.session}: {text}")

    for fire in fires:
        if fire.row is not None or fire.when is None or fire.when >= retained:
            fire.why = mismatch(fire, skews)
    mismatches = [(f, f.why) for f in fires if f.why]

    if not args.check:
        print(f"{len(fires)} fire(s) across {len(paths)} session(s), "
              f"{len(fires) - len(orphan_rows)} with a harness record, "
              f"{sum(1 for f in fires if f.row is not None)} with a run row\n")
        for line in render(sorted(fires, key=lambda f: (f.session, f.index))):
            print(line)
        if mismatches:
            print()
    for fire, why in mismatches:
        stamp = fire.when.isoformat(timespec="seconds") if fire.when else "?"
        print(f"mismatch: {fire.session[:8]} {stamp} {fire.hook or '?'}/{fire.event}: {why}")
    grouped = group_unattributed(unattributed)
    if grouped:
        print(f"\n{len(grouped)} unattributed text(s), by their first 40 characters:")
        for prefix, count in grouped:
            print(f"  {count:>4}  {prefix!r}")
    if args.check:
        print(f"\n{len(mismatches)} mismatch(es) over {len(fires)} fire(s) in "
              f"{len(paths)} session(s).")
        return 1 if mismatches else 0
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
